    "description": "Lumber camp (sawmill), level 2 of 3: L1 plus flourish 2. A miniature sawmill: a long open mill hall (dark oak frame on cobblestone feet, spruce roof with dark oak eaves and trim) with the saw bench in the middle, a sash-saw frame whose chain blade cuts the log on the carriage line; the grindstone (workstation) beside it. Log yard with piles and a pulley at the right end, plank yard at the left. L2 adds a waterwheel behind the hall driving the saw, a stonecutter, sawhorse, cart, lanterns, sign; L3 a drying rack, more logs, saplings, moss. Not yet builder-tested: stonecutter. Decoration step adds: sign_text, water.",
    "changes": "Rebuilt as a long open mill hall with the saw bench as the centrepiece (a sash-saw frame over the log line), a log yard on one end and plank stacks on the other, a two-tone roof with overhang and trim on a dark frame and cobblestone feet; each level adds something visible (L2 waterwheel, second saw, cart; L3 drying rack, saplings, more logs).",
